  "name": "Screech Formant Rise",
  "author": "Riddim Rack",
  "description": "A vocal screech: a vowel filter glides from an oh to an ee on every quarter note while the pitch bends upward, so it screams like a voice instead of a saw. Play short phrases around C3-C4 and let notes ring; it is mono and legato, and harder hits play louder and brighter. Macros: Rise sets how far the vowel travels; Vowel Start moves where it begins; Bend adds pitch glide into each note and brightens its edge; Grit drives the distortion harder and adds bite at a steady level.",
